# Deskflow Windows Build & Deploy

## Required workflow after code changes

After **any** change that affects the shipped product — C++/CMake, Tauri/React UI
(`ui/`), migrate/package scripts, or config that the installed app reads — run
**build → test → migrate → package → install** before considering the task done.
Do not stop at `cargo check` / `tsc` / `tauri:dev` alone when the user needs an
installed binary.

UI-only / Tauri-only still needs migrate (defaults rebuild Tauri) so
`C:\Program Files\Deskflow\deskflow.exe` matches the workspace. Skip C++ rebuild
only when core/daemon artifacts are already current:

```powershell
.\migrate-windows.ps1 -BuildFirst:$false -Force   # still builds Tauri by default
```

Full product path:

```powershell
# 1. Build (imports MSVC, vcpkg, Qt)
.\build-windows.ps1

# 2. Unit tests (reconfigure with -DSKIP_BUILD_TESTS=OFF first if tests are missing)
$env:PATH = "$PWD\.qt\6.10.3\msvc2022_64\bin;$PWD\build\bin;$env:PATH"
& build\src\unittests\server\SwitchDecisionTests.exe
& build\src\unittests\server\DisplayLayoutTests.exe
& build\src\unittests\server\EdgeGraphTests.exe
& build\src\unittests\server\SwitchEngineTests.exe

# 3. Stage/install locally so Program Files has core + Qt runtime (Tauri cutover)
#    Required before packaging: the portable zip is built from this tree.
Start-Process powershell -Verb RunAs -Wait -ArgumentList `
  "-NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Command `"cd '$PWD'; .\migrate-windows.ps1 -Force`""

# 4. Package a portable zip for this machine and remotes (no VS needed on target)
.\package-windows-portable.ps1

# 5. Install from the package (elevated). Prefer this over hand-copying files.
$pkg = Get-ChildItem .\dist\deskflow-*-win-x64-portable -Directory |
  Sort-Object LastWriteTime -Descending | Select-Object -First 1
Start-Process powershell -Verb RunAs -Wait -ArgumentList `
  "-NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Command `"cd '$($pkg.FullName)'; .\Install-Remote.ps1`""
```

On a **remote host** (no Visual Studio / build tools): copy the zip from `dist\`, extract, then run `Install-Remote.ps1` elevated. Also install VC++ Redistributable x64 and WebView2 once if missing.

## package-windows-portable.ps1

Builds `dist/deskflow-<version>-win-x64-portable.zip` from the current
`C:\Program Files\Deskflow` tree (after migrate). Includes Tauri GUI, core,
daemon, Qt DLLs/plugins, `qt.conf`, `Install-Remote.ps1`, and `README.md`.

```powershell
.\package-windows-portable.ps1
.\package-windows-portable.ps1 -SourceDir 'C:\Program Files\Deskflow'
.\package-windows-portable.ps1 -SkipZip   # folder only under dist\
```

## Install-Remote.ps1 (inside the portable folder)

Copies `Deskflow\` into `C:\Program Files\Deskflow`, registers/updates the
Deskflow Windows service, and starts it. **Admin required.** No VS/CMake/Qt SDK.

```powershell
# From the extracted portable folder:
.\Install-Remote.ps1
.\Install-Remote.ps1 -NoStart
.\Install-Remote.ps1 -NoService   # files only; launch deskflow.exe manually
```

## migrate-windows.ps1

Still used on the **build machine** to assemble a complete install (Tauri GUI +
`deskflow-core` + Qt via windeployqt) before packaging. Settings in
`%APPDATA%\Deskflow` are preserved.

**Defaults:** `-Force -UseTauriUi -BuildTauriUi -BuildFirst`.

| Flag | Default | When |
|------|---------|------|
| `-BuildFirst` | on | Run `build-windows.ps1` before copying (`-BuildFirst:$false` to skip) |
| `-UseTauriUi` | on | Cut over GUI to Tauri (`-UseTauriUi:$false` for legacy Qt) |
| `-BuildTauriUi` | on | Build Tauri UI first (`-BuildTauriUi:$false` to skip) |
| `-Force` | on | Skip client/server upgrade safety check |
| `-WhatIf` | off | Preflight only; no admin needed |
| `-NoStart` | off | Install but do not restart the service |

Tauri cutover **must** deploy Qt for `deskflow-core` (it still links Qt). Do not
strip `Qt6*.dll` / `plugins` from the install.

## Manual incremental build (agents)

**Always import MSVC before `cmake --build`.** Without `vcvars64.bat`, STL headers fail (`cstdint` missing).

```powershell
$vcvars = "C:\Program Files\Microsoft Visual Studio\2022\Community\VC\Auxiliary\Build\vcvars64.bat"
$envFile = Join-Path $env:TEMP "deskflow-vcvars.env"
cmd /c "`"$vcvars`" >nul 2>&1 && set" | Out-File $envFile -Encoding ascii
Get-Content $envFile | ForEach-Object { if ($_ -match '^([^=]+)=(.*)$') { Set-Item "env:$($matches[1])" $matches[2] } }
Remove-Item $envFile -Force

cmake --build build --target deskflow deskflow-core server SwitchDecisionTests DisplayLayoutTests EdgeGraphTests SwitchEngineTests -j 8
```

Then finish with migrate → package → `Install-Remote.ps1` as above. For UI-only
changes when C++ binaries are already current:

```powershell
cd ui; .\scripts\build-windows.ps1
cd ..
.\migrate-windows.ps1 -BuildFirst:$false -BuildTauriUi:$false -Force
.\package-windows-portable.ps1
# then elevated Install-Remote.ps1 from the new dist folder
```

## Key paths

| Artifact | Path |
|----------|------|
| GUI / core (built) | `build/bin/deskflow-ui.exe`, `deskflow-core.exe` |
| Installed | `C:\Program Files\Deskflow\` |
| Portable zip | `dist/deskflow-*-win-x64-portable.zip` |
| Migration backups | `.migration-backup/<timestamp>/` |
| Qt | `.qt/6.10.3/msvc2022_64` |

## Pitfalls

- PowerShell: use `;` not `&&`.
- New `.cpp` files need CMake reconfigure (GLOB mismatch).
- `Server.h`: qualify `deskflow::server::` types; no `using namespace` in headers.
- Packaging without a prior migrate that includes Qt will produce a broken core (`Qt6Widgets.dll` missing).
- Remote hosts need VC++ Redistributable x64 and WebView2; not Visual Studio.
